require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART reader-pages
ask: Are the supplied source prefix, absent context and full system instructions readable beyond the twelve-line preview, with terminal-safe display and no current-freshness claim?
resize: 120x36
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/no-ack-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 ⚠ CONFIRM · descriptor-declared effect | partial-confirmation
keys: End y
require-live-snap: 25 acknowledgePartial | partial-refused
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART no-ack
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART drift
paste-file: @ART/accept-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 ⚠ CONFIRM · descriptor-declared effect | drift-confirmation
keys: End y
require-live-snap: 25 Source changed since catalog generation | source-refused
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART drift-refused
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restore
paste-file: @ART/accept-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 ⚠ CONFIRM · descriptor-declared effect | exact-acceptance
expect: acknowledged: true
expect: This starts no model request or scan
expect-not: Esc dismiss
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART confirm-hidden
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 Esc dismiss | canceled-acceptance
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART confirm-canceled
ask: Does a new confirmation own the controls without an older error banner competing, while cancel restores that error and starts no acceptance or model work?
paste-file: @ART/accept-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 ⚠ CONFIRM · descriptor-declared effect | retry-acceptance
keys: End y
require-live-snap: 25 Taint catalog accepted | accepted
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART accepted
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART edit-active
submit: run taint-iris-next:catalog-read
require-live-snap: 25 Saved taint catalog is unreadable | unreadable-active
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART unreadable
paste-file: @ART/pinned-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Saved taint catalog | retained-pin
paste-file: @ART/replace-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 ⚠ CONFIRM · descriptor-declared effect | reviewed-replacement
expect: Expected active catalog
expect-not: Esc dismiss
keys: End y
require-live-snap: 25 Taint catalog accepted | replaced
paste-file: @ART/exhausted-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 allowance exhausted: 2 calls committed | exhausted
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exhausted
ask: Can the operator explicitly repair the active catalog while retaining the accepted version and exhausted request history, without regeneration or a fallback scan?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 15
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: logs
submit: run campaign:allowance {"investigationId":"owned-taint-catalog"}
require-live-snap: 25 Calls committed: 2/2 | restarted-accounting
paste-file: @ART/pinned-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Saved taint catalog | restarted-profile
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART pin-read
paste-file: @ART/replay-pin-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 SAVED OUTPUT | restarted-reader
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_reader.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
